{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'python3 /opt/alva/aep.py --help'","aggregated_output":"usage: aep.py [-h] --port PORT tool [kv ...]\n\nAEP tool CLI for mode C pilots. Thin wrapper over the ac_client.py gateway\nthat takes key=value arguments instead of a JSON string, so no shell quoting\nis needed: python aep.py --port <port> begin_transaction\nproject=C:\\path\\to\\alva.toml python aep.py --port <port> create_literal\ntype=string value=fsync_meta_dir python aep.py --port <port> create_call\nname=step args=<literal_revision> python aep.py --port <port> append_step\nfunction=store.commit.put_object step=<call_revision> python aep.py --port\n<port> check_transaction python aep.py --port <port> commit_transaction\nRepeatable keys: args=... -> list of call arguments (create_call) params=...\n-> flat list of parameter names (add_function; types default \"string\") See\nAEP_TOOLS.md for the full tool list.\n\npositional arguments:\n  tool\n  kv           key=value arguments\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help   show this help message and exit\n  --port PORT\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
